EXT. MAPLE HILL PARK - NEAR THE OLD FOUNTAIN - DUSK

The sun is low. The park is almost empty. A JOGGER runs past with a small dog. Two OLD MEN play chess on a bench, not talking.

LIN, 19, sets a phone on a tripod. She wears a bright yellow jacket. She checks the screen and fixes her hair.

Beside her stands KOFI, 20, her friend. He holds a ring light. He is nervous but he does not say it.

LIN
Okay. We start. Hello, my friends. Today we go to the haunted fountain.

KOFI
Why are we saying haunted?

LIN
Because people like it. More views.

KOFI
But nobody say this fountain is haunted.

LIN
Now they say.

She laughs. He does not. He looks at the dry stone fountain. He turns the ring light a little.

The Jogger is gone. The old men are gone too. The chessboard is still on the bench, pieces standing.

LIN (CONT'D)
(to the camera)
Is very quiet here. Very, very quiet.

KOFI
Lin. The men. They left the game.

LIN
So? They are tired.

KOFI
Maybe.

She taps the screen. She frowns. She taps again.

LIN
The video, it stops. Always the same place.

KOFI
Maybe the phone is cold.

LIN
Phones are not cold.

A cold wind moves over the grass. The fountain makes a small sound, like a drop of water falling. But the fountain is dry.

He steps back. She does not notice. She is still looking at the screen.

LIN (CONT'D)
(whispering)
Kofi. Look.

He comes closer. On the screen, behind her, there is someone in the water of the fountain. Only in the video. Not in the park.

KOFI
I do not see anything.

LIN
(her voice thin)
Yes you do.

He is silent. His hands shake on the ring light.

It is the last video they will make together.

She turns off the phone. Fast. She takes the tripod and walks to the path. He follows her. Neither of them looks back at the fountain.

The wind stops. The water drips once more.
